<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $50.7 mln June 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $50.7 mln June 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $50.7 million surplus on June 20 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 20</p>
<p>Exports: $273.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $232.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $241.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $232.3 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $50.7 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.438 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.981 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.809 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.378 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $112 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
